These reproduce the template codes, row and column codes, datapoint
identifiers, dimension and member labels, and the structure of the annotated
table layout published by the European Banking Authority for PAY 4.2
(FRPPAY 4.2), the payment and fraud reporting framework under PSD2.

The EBA legal notice states:

    "Reproduction of all EBA material on this site is authorised, provided the
    source is acknowledged, save where otherwise stated."
    -- https://www.eba.europa.eu/legal-notice

That is a permission conditional on attribution, not a named open licence. The
MIT licence in LICENSE does not extend to this material, and nothing here
relicenses it.

Source: EBA PAY 4.2 (FRPPAY 4.2) annotated table layout, 2026-01-06.


3. EBA DPM 2.0 database and anything derived from it — same terms
------------------------------------------------------------------

    source/dpm2/          (downloaded, gitignored)
    09-validation-rules.csv
    README_DPM2.md
    web/public/data/      (generated, gitignored)

The same clause covers these: the DPM database is published on the same site,
and neither its download pages nor the database itself states otherwise - the
only "copyright" in the model is a NACE activity label.

web/public/data is a reformatting rather than a copy. It holds template, row,
column, dimension, member, property and rule codes with their labels, the
datapoint identifiers, and which rows add up to which, written as parquet for a
browser to query. It is not the EBA's distribution and must not be presented as
one: the EBA publishes the database itself, and that is where a reporting
institution should get it.

Sources, by release:

    DPM 2.0 release 4.2.1   https://www.eba.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2026-02/
                            ad0d2577-a1eb-4826-a249-a1f7701c6796/DPM2%20Database_v_4_2_1.zip
    DPM 2.0 release 4.3     reporting framework 4.3, "DPM2 Database_v 4_3.zip"
    DPM 2.0 release 4.4     reporting framework 4.4, "DPM2 Database_v 4_4.zip" - a DRAFT
                            technical package, and anything built from it is a draft too

Between-release validation rule updates come from the validation rules packages
page and are applied with source/apply_vr_updates.py; a published copy says in
its manifest which release it was built from and when.

This repository is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or published by the EBA.
The labels are transcribed verbatim and carry no interpretation; for the
regulatory definitions and the validation rules see the EBA Guidelines on
fraud reporting under PSD2 (EBA/GL/2018/05, as amended).
